---
description: AI assistant (chatbot) feature — portal drawer + Python ai-service
globs:
  - "apps/ecom-portal/src/features/assistant/**"
  - "apps/ecom-portal/src/mocks/assistant.handlers.ts"
  - "apps/ecom-portal/vite-assistant-proxy.ts"
  - "apps/ai-service/**"
alwaysApply: false
---
- Source of truth for request/response/events: apps/ai-service/CONTRACT.md. Never invent fields.
- Frontend follows apps/ecom-portal/ECOM-PORTAL-FEATURE-BLUEPRINT.md and .cursor/rules/agenct.md
  (AppDrawer/AppButton/useToast/useConfirm from @solverminds/shared-ui, no inline style, no hex colours, no `any`).
- The browser runs tools by calling EXISTING feature api functions (bookingApi, trackingApi, schedulesApi, ...).
  Never add new backend endpoints for tools; never call fixtures/bridges directly from the assistant.
- Default assistant mode never submits a booking — it prefills via useBookingStore + buildMasterDetailsFromSchedule.
- Automation mode may submit only after explicit user confirm on AutomationConfirmCard → actions/submit-booking.action.ts (guardrail allowlist).
- All assistant HTTP goes to same-origin /api/assistant/* . Never call the AI service URL directly from the browser.
- Python: FastAPI + anthropic SDK, pydantic v2 models for every request/event, async everywhere, no DB connection to ecom data.
- Never log or persist the Authorization token.
